CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model reg:observe
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
CALL observe
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
A volatile write model observes the written value: the write is routed to a
call of the model, which can assert on the value. Verification succeeds because
the model is called with the value written in main; it is not invoked for the
zero-initialisation of the global (INITIALIZE_FUNCTION writes are not treated as
device actions), which would otherwise fail the assertion.
